# These example reports are pinned by their exact byte hashes in the paired manifest.
examples/evaluation/*.json text eol=lf
# The window's page is built by Vite with LF line endings and committed; CI rebuilds it on Windows and requires the
# result byte-identical to the checkout, so the checkout must not be converted to CRLF there.
src/spec_surgeon/web/static/** text eol=lf
# The page's sources are the build's input: checked out with CRLF they would reach the built index.html, which is
# compared byte for byte with the Linux build.
frontend/** text eol=lf
# The guided tour's showcase is compared byte for byte with its builder (tests/test_tutorial.py) and with the
# installed wheel (packaging/installed_wheel_smoke.py); its plain-text members (the refused table of contents, the
# table of values) must not be converted to CRLF on a Windows checkout.
src/spec_surgeon/examples/tutorial/** binary
